# on-read-reminder -- rules
#
# Each rule maps a gitignore-style pattern to the file(s) the agent should
# read when it reads a matching path. Lines that don't parse are reported
# (and ignored) instead of failing silently.
#
#   <pattern> -> <file>[, <file>...]   remind the agent to read <file>(s)
#   !<pattern>                         never remind for these paths
#
# Patterns are gitignore-style, matched against the project-relative path:
#
#   *    any run of characters within one path segment
#   ?    a single character within one path segment
#   **   any number of path segments (a/**/b also matches a/b)
#
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored at the project root; one without
# a slash matches the file's basename at any depth. A trailing slash targets
# a directory and everything under it.
#
# Rules apply top to bottom: a matching "->" line adds its file(s) to the
# reminder; a matching "!" line clears everything matched so far, and later
# lines can add again. Reminder paths are relative to the project root.
#
# Examples:
#
#   server/**/models/**          -> docs/GLOSSARY.md
#   shared/**/models/**          -> docs/GLOSSARY.md
#   desktop/client/**/models/**  -> docs/GLOSSARY.md
#   **/*.sql                     -> docs/DB-CONVENTIONS.md, docs/GLOSSARY.md
#   !vendor/**
